commit 2ad1f09
The fold of adjacent markers follows Isabelle: the later marker applies

Plan section 1b. The fold pattern was a marker followed by any character, so
two adjacent markers matched as a pair, folded nothing, and the second never
folded with what followed: one marker folded, two did not, three folded the
last. Isabelle's renderers let the later control symbol apply and emit the
displaced one literally. The pattern is now a marker followed by a non-marker
(never a line break), which does the same: x\<^sub>\<^sub>1 renders x⇩₁.

Granted by the author on 2026-09-22 on the review's proposal. Measured: no
rendering in the 4,506-file corpus changes (the construction occurs in no
source here or in the checked-in mirrors); the seeded cases state the new
rule for two kinds of marker and for a marker before a line break.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 6c1ee40
symbol_explode lives beside the escape pattern whose rule it shares

The indexed view's contract is stated in symbol_explode's unit, and the two
scans encode the same naming rule with symbol_explode the more permissive; the
function now sits ten lines from _ESCAPE and its docstring states the superset
relation pretty_unicode_indexed relies on. tokens.py imports it from unicode.py,
which lets position.py's only deferred intra-package import be hoisted;
position.py keeps re-exporting symbol_explode for its outside importers
(review item C38).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 601df27
SUBSUP_RESTORE_TABLE is derived from the fold table, which must stay injective

The inverse was a second hand-written copy of 142 entries; a one-sided edit
restored a silently different symbol (review item C12, measured with an added
entry). Derived now, and the module refuses to load if the forward table ever
folds two pairs to one character.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 615cb01
Review conditions applied: record only rewritten matches, name the record, close the net

The adversarial review of 3360162 (ai-artifacts/UNICODE_REVIEW_2026-09-22.md)
ruled MET_ON_CONDITION. Applied here, with the author's two rulings of
2026-09-22:

- The recording keeps only the matches a replacement rewrote, so _map_offsets
  no longer infers "the text did not change" from "the length did not change"
  (sound before only because the fold table maps two characters to one, which
  nothing stated); the convention has two cases, and the match record is a
  named tuple read by field.
- The symbol table is read by field name everywhere; the public 4-tuple is a
  named projection, so the record's field order no longer silently decides
  what pretty_unicode does. The fold's marker class is derived from the fold
  table. _load_symbols is a pure function; _load_table takes its file list, so
  the test fixture goes through the real loader. pretty_unicode_indexed is
  annotated, so passing a string is a pyright error at the caller.
- FileIndex's ASCII prefix sums come from accumulate, the line starts from the
  sums, so two of the four corruptions the review found cannot be written.
- The suite: the corpus arm compares renderings, not lengths; a seed corpus in
  the seed table's alphabet is swept on every machine, so an empty sweep cannot
  pass; every symbol away from a fold owns its slice of the rendering; the six
  coordinate conversions and the ASCII bookkeeping are asserted per line and
  per file; each _ESCAPE match must be exactly one symbol; the two population
  counts travel with their own denominators; the position.py mutants are linear
  and self-contained; --self-check first runs an unmutated copy; fourteen
  mutants, all killed; the suite fails against the parent's FileIndex with no
  corpus present.
- Plan: the two-case convention, the review paragraph, the pre-fix-tree note,
  the corrected counts and citations; the review scripts declared frozen.

pretty_unicode stays byte-identical over the 4,506-file corpus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


